{"id":"000VWM","title":"Mystery Islands","author":"Killer Joe","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-06T02:31:17+00:00","posted":"Heute, 02:52 Uhr","rules":"Hello.\n\nI've been wanting to make another 'Islands' puzzle for a while, as a follow-up to Modular Islands and Entropic Islands, both of which are rated 2 stars for difficulty.\n\nWorking with unknown sets turned out to be a really fun and interesting setting experience. Rather than using our beloved Kropki dots, as I did in the previous two puzzles, I decided to lean much more heavily into the geometry and negative constraint. These are used to force groups and digits into the grid, making this puzzle a little more challenging. However, the logic is always fair.\n\nClick image to play in SudokuPad\n\nNormal Sudoku rules apply.\n\nDivide the digits 1-9 into 3 distinct 'mystery sets' of 3 digits each. Which digits belong to each set is to be determined by the solver.\n\nA digit placed in a circle indicates the size of the orthogonally connected group of cells that ALL contain digits from the same mystery set as that digit.\n\nNo group contains more than one circled cell.\nNot all groups contain a circle.\n\nDigits separated by a red diamond must not have a 2:1 ratio.\n\nHave fun.","solutionCode":"Row 9, first 6 digits.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/bnynpr8379","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/bnynpr8379","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-06T02:31:17+00:00"}